{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/873633-2ed-jump-system-broken","id":873633,"title":"[2ed] Jump system broken","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-25T02:49:51-07:00","id":873633,"title":"[2ed] Jump system broken","content":"Hi all,<br /> I know that this kind of topic has already been done, but I didn't find somethign really satisfactory and, furthemore, I just want to pick down all your house rules or mechanics about jumps in one topic.<br /> The CofD says that a character jumps Strenght+athletics meters divided by 3 (or feet) without distinction between vertical, horizontal and running jump. So a very good athlete, with Strenght 4 Athletics 4 usually rolls 3-4 successes which means only one meter of distance jumped.<br /> Now, for a vertical jump it is ok and realistic but, for an horizontal jump, especially with the run-up, it's completely unrealistic. I play volleyball in a C series and I can jump an average distance of 3,5 meters in an horizontal jump without run-up, and I'm not an olimpionic athlete.<br /> How do you deal with this mechanic? It becomes important especially for someone with vigor.<br /> Is there a more realistic and good working mechanic?<br /> Even doubling the meters jumped in a run-up horizontal jump is not enough with this kind of rules. The jumps would allows to travel an average distance of 2 meter that is already far from a realistic situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T03:10:44-07:00","id":873639,"title":"","content":"What you could do is go abstract. Instead of getting so far per success, make it a regular roll requiring one success with a penalty based on how far they're trying to go. And then with vigor just adjust what distance causes what penalty by an appropriate multiplier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T03:29:42-07:00","id":873643,"title":"","content":"I agree with Elfive. Just decide how difficult it is as a jump, and assign it as a penalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T04:06:51-07:00","id":873655,"title":"","content":"Mh ok I agree with your point of view. have you any suggestion about how determinate theese penality according with the stats of the character? I mean: Someone with strenght+athletics 8 should have less penality then a average human. I think I should determine an average distance related that dice pool and, then, confronting it with the distance of the leap. But again, how to determinate this average distance? And how take in account Vigor?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T04:23:19-07:00","id":873663,"title":"","content":"For a Vigor user, the jump distance is [successes * (Vigor+1)] yards or meters. Which would mean Vigor multiplies jump distance twice - first by three, then by dots+1...<br /> <br /> I have a feeling the way jumping was <i>meant</i> to work was successes meters/yards for a horizontal jump and successes feet or successes/3 meters for a vertical jump, with Vigor multiplying both values by dots+1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T04:43:00-07:00","id":873670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/873633-2ed-jump-system-broken?p=873655#post873655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone with strenght+athletics 8 should have less penality then a average human.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No, they shouldn't. What Strength + Athletics 8 gives them is a bigger chance of succeeding at a given penalty. They have about even odds of pulling off a -5 jump. someone with strength + athletics 4 does not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T05:10:47-07:00","id":873675,"title":"","content":"I see. <br /> Considering the suggestion of Morangias, what do you think about this:<br /> <br /> Vertical Jump: (strength+athletics)/3 that means 1 meter with the stats considered in the example<br /> Horizontal Jump: Strenght+Atheltics resulting in a 3-4 meters of jump that could be ok<br /> Run-up Horizontal Jump: (strenght+Athletics)+size meters; resulting in 8-9 meters that is in line with reality.<br /> <br /> With Vigor just multiply that distance for vigor+1 for each kind of jump with the exception of run-up jump:<br /> <br /> Run-up Jump with Vigor: [(strength+Athletics)*(Vigor+1)]+Size","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T06:06:44-07:00","id":873697,"title":"","content":"IMO the run up is best represented with a dice bonus to the roll. Don't overthink it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T06:23:22-07:00","id":873703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/873633-2ed-jump-system-broken?p=873655#post873655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mh ok I agree with your point of view. have you any suggestion about how determinate theese penality according with the stats of the character? I mean: Someone with strenght+athletics 8 should have less penality then a average human. I think I should determine an average distance related that dice pool and, then, confronting it with the distance of the leap. But again, how to determinate this average distance? And how take in account Vigor?</div> </div> </div> </div> Umm.... why should you have less of a penalty? Everyone should have the same penalty, but those with a high Str+Athl dice pool will have more dice to roll and a higher chance fo success. There's no need to calculate distances or anything. It all comes down to &quot;how difficult do I want this jump to be from a story point of view.&quot; <br /> <br /> Can I ask how often jumps come up in your game? This seems like a whole lot of detail for something I haven't seen come up that often.<br /> <br /> As for Vigor? I don't see any reason to add that in beyond the extra Strength dots with regular jumping. That's the beauty of using a simplifed system. If a player wants to use active jumping, technically its not allowed, but I think it could be fun to say you can jump a number of floors equal to 1/2 dots rounded up. So, with three dots of Vigor, you could jump to the top of a two story building with a point of vitae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T06:53:32-07:00","id":873721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/873633-2ed-jump-system-broken?p=873703#post873703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I ask how often jumps come up in your game? This seems like a whole lot of detail for something I haven't seen come up that often.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so often but sometime it could happen. For example it happened in the last game while the PCs fled away by the rooftops. Or sometime happens that a PC try a jump to reach the windows of someone. As I said, it's not frequent but it can happen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/873633-2ed-jump-system-broken?p=873703#post873703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Vigor? I don't see any reason to add that in beyond the extra Strength dots with regular jumping. That's the beauty of using a simplifed system. If a player wants to use active jumping, technically its not allowed, but I think it could be fun to say you can jump a number of floors equal to 1/2 dots rounded up. So, with three dots of Vigor, you could jump to the top of a two story building with a point of vitae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok just a question: why use active (a point of vitae) Vigor if its passive effect already allow to increase the jump by itself? I could agree on the mechanic you exposed but it should be free in my opinion.<br /> Anyway I'm according with your rule also because it is in line with my proposed system (even if I admit mine is more complicated :P). In fact with Vigor 3 and the stats proposed above, the PC should be able to jump vertically 1*4 meters and reach an height - adding the average human height with the arms raised (2,4 meters) - of 6,5 rounded at 7 meters (a second floor of a building).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T07:04:23-07:00","id":873727,"title":"","content":"I mean, if you really wanted to be rigorous you could take the vertical height a character would achieve by RAW, factor in their speed (which is handily in feet per second) and then work out the parabolic arc they would travel to determine the distance they can cover. It's a bit of work but you could probably make a spreadsheet to figure it out. I actually did something similar for a university project involving a miniature trebuchet once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T07:18:58-07:00","id":873737,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm graduated in engineering too and I know that the range of an object launched is due to the starting velocity but, in an human jump, it's not so simply XD<br /> in fact a sprinter doesen't jump more then a jumper and a jumper doesen't reach his full speed during the run-up. The explosive strenght exerted by the legs is more important then the velocity of the run (that is still important but not the only factor) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T07:50:43-07:00","id":873754,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but we can fudge that bit. It's only a game, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T08:12:06-07:00","id":873762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/873633-2ed-jump-system-broken?p=873721#post873721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not so often but sometime it could happen. For example it happened in the last game while the PCs fled away by the rooftops. Or sometime happens that a PC try a jump to reach the windows of someone. As I said, it's not frequent but it can happen.</div> </div> </div> </div> I just don't understand why you want such a complex system for something that only happens occasionally. If its more fun for your group, more power to you, but my personal experience is having to pause the game to go look up rules you don't remember tends to sap the fun more than it engages it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ok just a question: why use active (a point of vitae) Vigor if its passive effect already allow to increase the jump by itself? I could agree on the mechanic you exposed but it should be free in my opinion. </div> </div> </div> Because the suggestion I made puts the default one to shame? A single story is roughly 10 feet. With Vigor 5, you'd need 2 successes to make a single floor. 4 to make a second floor. That's a bit extreme, requiring huge amount of successes AND max Vigor? I'm suggesting a single vitae can give you the equivalent of an exceptional success at Vigor 1 and take out the guessing.<br /> <br /> If you want that for free, by all means. I just thought it felt a bit out of line between the free and cost benefits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T08:13:32-07:00","id":873763,"title":"","content":"What if I want to play a vampire and not a kangaroo though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T08:32:14-07:00","id":873775,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I figured that the second use of Active Vigor means &quot;Do something narratively awesome related to Strength&quot;, like ripping floor safes out of the floor, leaping tall buildings in a single bound, or holding the trash compactor open just a few more seconds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T08:51:12-07:00","id":873792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/873633-2ed-jump-system-broken?p=873762#post873762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I just don't understand why you want such a complex system for something that only happens occasionally. If its more fun for your group, more power to you, but my personal experience is having to pause the game to go look up rules you don't remember tends to sap the fun more than it engages it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, chases, veichles crash and even combat in not action session are quite rare, but their mechanics are not so simple<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/873633-2ed-jump-system-broken?p=873762#post873762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the suggestion I made puts the default one to shame? A single story is roughly 10 feet. With Vigor 5, you'd need 2 successes to make a single floor. 4 to make a second floor. That's a bit extreme, requiring huge amount of successes AND max Vigor? I'm suggesting a single vitae can give you the equivalent of an exceptional success at Vigor 1 and take out the guessing.<br /> <br /> If you want that for free, by all means. I just thought it felt a bit out of line between the free and cost benefits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, do not confuse heigth of the jump (from the earth to the foot) with the height reached. According to that system with just two successes you can jump 0.6 meters that multiplied for 6 (vigor +1) is 3.6 meters. Adding the average height of a man with raised arms (2.3 -2.4) you can grab something at 6 meters (a second floor).<br /> <br /> Anyway I thought to this home rule that should simplify a little the things:<br /> <br /> The base system is:<br /> <br /> Vertical Jump: (strength+Vigor+athletics successes/3)*(Vigor+1) in meters<br /> Horizontal Jump: (Strenght+Vigor+Atheltics successes)*(Vigor+1) in meters<br /> Run-up Horizontal Jump: (strenght+Vigor+Athletics successes)*(Vigor+1) +size in meters<br /> <br /> BUT, If the situation is not excited (not chases) and you can &quot;take your time&quot; for the jump, you don't need to roll and automatically consider half the pool for the jump (rounded down) as successes in order to establish the distance.<br /> On the countrary, in a frantic situation, you need to roll the dice pool due to the fact that you couldn't properly evalutate the distances or you jump too soon/late. In this way could be justified a ridicolous distance.<br /> <br /> I think this isn't too complicated in comparision with the average rules (combat, chases etc). If you are not in trouble you don't need to roll just multiply half the pool for Vigor+1 and add size for run-up or divide by 3 for vertical jump. These are the meters jumped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 04-25-2016, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T09:50:24-07:00","id":873837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/873633-2ed-jump-system-broken?p=873763#post873763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if I want to play a vampire and not a kangaroo though?</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you are <i>dumb</i> and <i>wrong</i> and aren't playing Kangaroo: The Requiem like the rest of us.<br /> <br /> Pfft, who ever heard about playing something silly like vampires?<br /> <hr /><br /> I personally am of the mind that jumping should just be a simple calculation; divide your Strength + Athletics by 3 to get the long jump in yards, the high jump in feet, and use your full Strength + Athletics for a running jump.<br /> <br /> You'd only roll Strength + Athletics if there was a question of whether or not you could make the jump.<br /> <br /> Yes, this means that Mr. Average Kangaroo, with a base Strength of 2, Athletics of 2, and Vigor 5 would be able to long jump 18 yards, high jump 6 yards, and could jump 54 yards on a running jump.<br /> <br /> His sister, Ms. Maxine Kangaroo, has a base Strength of 10, Athletics of 10, and Vigor 5. She can long jump 50 yards, high jump 16 yards and change, and could clear 150 yards on a running jump. In other words, she can easily leapfrog 3 buses parked end to end, and could comfortably jump over a football field.<br /> <br /> You know, so she could box someone.<br /> <br /> Because that's what kangaroos do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T10:26:06-07:00","id":873856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/873633-2ed-jump-system-broken?p=873792#post873792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, chases, veichles crash and even combat in not action session are quite rare, but their mechanics are not so simple<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> I've found that, in Werewolf, chases and combat are actually fairly common. In fact, I remember that the developers specifcially said Chase rules were designed with Werewolf in mind. I've found that Hunter games include a lot of combat, and several players have used cars as weapons on a frequent basis. As well, there are people who have a lot of combat and chases in Vampire, depending on their style of game. Jumping, meanwhile, has never been a concern in any game I've played, Vampire or otherwise. Further, all three of these examples are used in contested situations.<br /> <br /> The needs of a houserule for jumping are completely different.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wait, do not confuse heigth of the jump (from the earth to the foot) with the height reached </div> </div> </div>I didn't. I merely didn't feel it appropriate to assume there was something to grab that wouldn't break under one's weight. On my home, there's no such option - you either land feet on the roof, or you fall back to the ground. <br /> <br /> <br /> Have fun with your game. I'm out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T10:36:19-07:00","id":873863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/873633-2ed-jump-system-broken#post873633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi all,<br /> I know that this kind of topic has already been done, but I didn't find somethign really satisfactory and, furthemore, I just want to pick down all your house rules or mechanics about jumps in one topic.<br /> The CofD says that a character jumps Strenght+athletics meters divided by 3 (or feet) without distinction between vertical, horizontal and running jump. So a very good athlete, with Strenght 4 Athletics 4 usually rolls 3-4 successes which means only one meter of distance jumped.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems to be an abbreviation of previous rules. In other books, for every success you jumped one foot vertically. Horizontal jumps were different, depending upon standing and getting a running lead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>World of Darkness</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A character can jump one foot vertically for each success gained on a jumping roll. In a standing broad jump, a character can cross two feet per success rolled. In a running jump, a character can cross a number of feet equal to her Size + four more feet per success rolled.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T16:19:02-07:00","id":876097,"title":"","content":"Generally I don't care but, if I would it would probably allow you being able to jump up to that upper floor in front that building so you could eventually climb your way to the top or jumping from a building to another during a chase; In both cases I would probably assume that past Vigor X it would be automatic and that if your Vigor is below you would need a roll and if your Vigor is too low you wouldn't make it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T17:14:49-07:00","id":876127,"title":"","content":"I agree with applying bonuses for a running start (+1 for each turn you spend running, up to +3) and penalties for distance (-1 to -5). There can be other sources of bonuses and penalties, like an improvised jumping pole and poor visibility. One Success is all that is needed. That requires a lot less calculation and keeps the game flowing, which should be a priority. You also apply your dots in Vigor to your Strength, as usual. Let's not forget Willpower expenditure and the Parkour Style. Those can save your life in this scenario.<br /> <br /> As for using Active Vigor to jump, I agree with this post:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/873633-2ed-jump-system-broken?p=873775#post873775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I figured that the second use of Active Vigor means &amp;quot;Do something narratively awesome related to Strength&amp;quot;, like ripping floor safes out of the floor, leaping tall buildings in a single bound, or holding the trash compactor open just a few more seconds.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}